# MODIFIED-PAGE-KEYS: a page key held with a modifier is fx v0.0.16's
# composer move to a page (escape_parser.zig:169-173, :708-709@481104fd),
# which the full transcript does not take (input_full_transcript_runtime.zig:
# 156-178): it goes on to the composer behind the screen and moves the caret
# a page. p5-transcript-md's answer makes the document taller than the
# screen, and a four-row draft waits in the composer. Ctrl-O; Ctrl-PgUp in
# the tilde spelling and in the keypad's (the screen stays at its tail); the
# bare PgUp (it pages); Escape; and an X typed where the caret is: the first
# row, where the held keys took it, not the last, where it was.
gateway p5-transcript-md-turns.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
env TZ=UTC
wait 4
type show me the list
wait 1
key Enter
wait 12
snap answered
type one
key C-j
type two
key C-j
type three
key C-j
type four
wait 0.5
snap draft
key C-o
wait 2
snap full
key -H 1b 5b 35 3b 35 7e
wait 1
snap full-ctrl-pgup
key -H 1b 5b 35 37 34 32 31 3b 35 75
wait 1
snap full-kp-ctrl-pgup
key PPage
wait 1
snap full-pgup
key Escape
wait 1
snap closed
type X
wait 0.5
snap typed
gwlog
